# Never let the SPA fallback answer an /assets/* request.
#
# /assets/* is served `Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable`.
# With a bare `/* /index.html 200` catch-all, a request for a hashed chunk that
# hasn't propagated yet is answered with index.html at HTTP 200 — so the browser
# caches an HTML body under a .js URL, as immutable, FOR A YEAR. Every later load
# then fails with "Failed to fetch dynamically imported module" and no amount of
# refreshing fixes it, because `immutable` tells the browser not to revalidate.
# That is what left a QA on a black screen for two days in Aug 2026.
#
# A genuine 404 fails cleanly instead: the import rejects, lazyWithRetry /
# ErrorBoundary fire, and hardRecoverReload() purges and reloads.
#
# The target is deliberately NOT named 404.html: Cloudflare Pages treats a
# literal 404.html as the site-wide not-found page, which overrides the
# catch-all below and makes every non-root path 404 instead of loading the
# app. Naming it something else keeps the SPA fallback intact.
#
# Real files are unaffected — Cloudflare Pages serves static assets BEFORE
# applying redirect rules, so this only ever catches assets that don't exist.
/assets/*  /_asset-missing.html  404
/*         /index.html  200
